      "writtenOn": "2026-11-20T13:11:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Addressed the predictable boundary case by checking the EEPROM capacity at the discovered offset before writing. \nIf the FRU does not fit, the write is rejected before any bytes are written. Added tests for an exact fit and writes exceeding capacity. \nIf an unexpected short write still occurs, it is detected and reported; this cannot undo bytes already written, so a rescan is not treated as rollback",
      "parentUuid": "f0215600_c411aa02",
      "revId": "713518c44ca80dc13aaef2a6ae4501115584baff",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
